## Model Routing (Hard Rule)

This repo must define **which model/tool does what**. The coordinator must obey this routing policy, and workers must not “do everything” in one window.

```yaml
model_routing:
  analysis:
    engine: codex
    model: gpt-5.2-thinking # default; override per repo if needed
    notes: "Planning, root-cause analysis, verification reasoning"

  execution:
    engine: claude-code
    model: claude-opus-4.5 # default; override per repo if needed
    notes: "Coding + task execution (apply patches, run commands, implement fixes)"

  data_processing:
    engine: gemini
    model: gemini-3 # default; override per repo if needed
    notes: "Normalize/chunk/summarize large artifacts before handing to other models"

agent_work_type_defaults:
  # Optional: lets the coordinator auto-fill work_type/execution_engine in task briefs.
  # If omitted, default by phase (0/1/4 = analysis; 1.5/2/3/5/6 = execution).
  coordinator: analysis
  intake-agent: analysis
  product-agent: analysis
  researcher-agent: analysis
  security-agent: analysis
  ai-sast-agent: analysis
  evals-agent: analysis
  testing-agent: analysis
  qa-agent: analysis
  code-review-agent: analysis
  logging-agent: analysis
  sre-agent: analysis
  availability-agent: analysis
  ui-validation-agent: analysis
  ux-audit-agent: analysis

  api-contract-agent: execution
  data-agent: execution
  infra-agent: execution
